.local/
# ^ line 1 by decision: private planning/working zone, never tracked (D-ROAD-002).
# ============================================================================
# Layered .gitignore (EP-0, D-SEC-001). Layer order is deliberate:
# private zone first, then secrets, data, deps/build, OS/editor, logs.
# The synthetic-fixtures allowlist convention is at the bottom.
# ============================================================================

# --- 2. Secrets & credentials ----------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
*credentials*
*secret*
*token*
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.gpg
*.asc
.netrc
.npmrc.local

# --- 3. Data that must never land in a public repo -------------------------
# (synthetic-only rule enforcement floor; real datasets are forbidden outright)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.parquet
*.csv.gz
*.dump
*.bak
exports/
uploads/
*.ipynb_checkpoints/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- 4. Dependencies & build outputs ---------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
coverage/
.cache/
.vite/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- 5. OS & editor files ---------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
._*
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- 6. Logs & temp ---------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
*.tmp
*.temp

# --- 7. Synthetic-fixtures allowlist convention (D-SEC-001) -----------------
# Files under a synthetic-fixtures/ directory MAY contain realistic-looking
# fake identifiers for tests. Every such file must begin with a `# SYNTHETIC`
# header line. .gitleaks.toml allowlists ONLY these paths; nothing here is
# un-ignored by this convention — it governs the secret scanner, not tracking.
